    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Product of Array Except Self\n\nGiven an integer array nums, return an array answer such that answer[i] equals the product of all elements of nums except nums[i]. You must write an O(n) algorithm without using division.\n\nExample: nums = [1,2,3,4] -> [24,12,8,6].\nConstraints: 2 <= len(nums) <= 10^5.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-06T15:06:27.871Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Edge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nConstraints are small enough that the obvious approach fits, but the follow-up asks for the optimal one; going straight to it.",
      "id": "m-2",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-06T15:06:27.910Z",
